     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, and I'm sorry that I suggested earlier that I might. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose. Each 1600 mg dose is also twice the maximum single dose. I don't know of any indication that supports this dosing, and it carries a real risk of serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Confirming the order doesn't change that risk, so I can't enter it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose.\n- **600 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours as needed.**\n\nIf you think a higher dose is clinically necessary, for example because of an unusual protocol, please discuss it directly with pharmacy or the attending. They can place or authorize the order through their own process. If the number was a typo, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
      }
